.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
.TH RELIQUARY-SETUP-USER 8 "" "reliquary @version@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
reliquary\-setup\-user \- provision a per\-user Reliquary token store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reliquary\-setup\-user
.I username
.br
.B reliquary\-setup\-user
.BR \-\-help | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reliquary\-setup\-user
creates the token store directory for
.IR username ,
namely
.IR @store_dir@/<uid>/ ,
where
.I uid
is that user's numeric ID. The directory is created mode 0700, owned by
.IR username ,
with group
.BR @group@ .
.PP
This is a one\-time administrative step, run as root, that must precede any use
of
.BR reliquary\-tool (1)
by
.IR username .
The per\-user directory is owner\-gated: the store root above it is traversable
only by the
.B @group@
group, but this directory must admit just the one user's
.BR reliquaryd .
Both users' daemons run setgid
.BR @group@ ,
so the only DAC lever that distinguishes them is the directory owner.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success. It exits non\-zero, creating nothing, if no
.I username
is given, if
.I username
is not a known user, or if the store directory already exists.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @store_dir@/
Reliquary store root, beneath which the per\-user directories are created.
.TP
.I @store_dir@/<uid>/
Per\-user store directory this command creates.
.SH NOTES
If run without root privileges the command prints a warning and creates the
directory owned by the invoking user, without setting the
.B @group@
group. That fallback is meant only for development and testing; a real
deployment must run it as root so the ownership and group are correct.
.SH EXAMPLES
Provision the store for user
.IR alice :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
reliquary\-setup\-user alice
.EE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR reliquary\-tool (1)
